  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 148 AM MDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nToday through Sun...Upper level trough moving through southern \nCanada will dig far enough south to increase wind in southern \nIdaho today to significant thresholds for Fire Weather. A closed\nlow that develops off the end of this trough slowly meanders \nonshore and moves through the ID panhandle and western MT Sat \nnight and Sun. Wind appears even stronger on Sun when the close \nlow's southeast corner overlays the entire forecast area. \n\nThe closer the low gets, the cooler temperatures will be. Thus\ntoday will be the warmest overall. Temperatures cool slightly on\nFri, then level off on Sat, then cool down 14 to 20 deg F from\nSat afternoon to Sun afternoon.\n\nThe trough passing by today does appear to entrain some moisture\nnorthward into the southern and eastern highlands in the\nforecast area by late tonight into Fri morning. A slight chance\nof thunderstorms develops in the southeast corner of the\nforecast area. By Sat and Sun, showers and thunderstorms will\noverspread the forecast area, with Sat having the greatest\ncoverage, then the pattern shifting eastward and mostly out of\nthe central Idaho mountains. \n\nSun night through Wed...Dry zonal flow sets up in the wake of\nthe upper level low. This will mean are return to warming,\ngetting to near climatic normals by Tue afternoon. The moderate\nto strong upper level westerly flow will mean gusty afternoons\nas inversions break. Dewpoints will fall, and so critical fire\nweather conditions may return for some of the zones during this\nperiod.",
